functionDeclarations.description:
Propose asset.undoplaceservice for review; never apply it to the live books. Undo placing an asset in service while nothing has happened to it since; do not use it to change depreciation by hand.
Example input: {"assetId":"asset_123"}
CONFLICT: Depreciation or another change was posted since. Undo that later work first.

Propose asset.undotransfer for review; never apply it to the live books. Undo the latest move of a fixed asset while its date is open; do not use it to edit the asset by hand.
Example input: {"assetId":"asset_123"}
NOT_FOUND: The asset is not in this workspace. Check the asset in this workspace.

Propose bill.spreadundo for review; never apply it to the live books. Undo spreading a bill over months while none of its months is closed; do not use it to void the bill.
Example input: {"billId":"bill_123"}
CONFLICT: The bill is not spread, or one of its months is closed. Reopen the month first, or spread a bill that is spread.

Propose inventory.landedcostundo for review; never apply it to the live books. Undo a landed cost, reversing its entry and its stock moves together; do not use it to undo an ordinary bill or journal entry.
Example input: {"entryId":"landed-cost-abc123"}
NOT_FOUND: That entry is not a landed cost of this workspace. Check the entry id.

Propose invoice.spreadundo for review; never apply it to the live books. Undo spreading an invoice over months while none of its months is closed; do not use it to void the invoice.
Example input: {"invoiceId":"invoice_123"}
CONFLICT: The invoice is not spread, or one of its months is closed. Reopen the month first, or spread an invoice that is spread.

Propose presence.leave for review; never apply it to the live books. Take this person out of the collaborator list; do not use it to remove anyone else — the row deleted is always the caller’s own.
Example input: {}
NOT_A_MEMBER: The caller is not a member of the workspace. Open a workspace the person belongs to.

Propose reportschedule.preview for review; never apply it to the live books. Show the report email a schedule would send, before it is saved; nothing is sent.
Example input: {"report":"pl","frequency":"monthly"}
FORBIDDEN: The caller is a bookkeeper or a viewer. Ask an owner or an accountant.

Propose user.aikeyremove for review; never apply it to the live books. Remove the AI provider key saved on your own account; do not use it to change anyone else's.
Example input: {}
UNAUTHENTICATED: Nobody is signed in. Sign in and try again.

Propose user.aikeyset for review; never apply it to the live books. Save your own AI provider key so the assistant uses your account; do not use it to change a workspace setting.
Example input: {"apiKey":"AIza..."}
INVALID_INPUT: The key is empty or not a string. Send the key as a non-empty string.

Propose watches.remove for review; never apply it to the live books. Stop receiving change notices for a record you watch; do not use this to delete the record itself.
Example input: {"watchId":"watch_123"}
NOT_FOUND: The watch is not yours or no longer exists. Reload your watch list and choose one of your active watches.
